# @afenda/feature-__MODULE_ID__

Canonical architecture: **ARCH-1002** §6–§8 · Scaffold: `packages/_scaffold/feature`.

## Public doors (only root-level exceptions)

- `src/index.ts` — neutral
- `src/client.ts` — browser-safe
- `src/server.ts` — server-only (imports `@afenda/kernel/server`)
- `src/metadata.ts` — governed metadata, no tenant I/O

## Flat layout (required for new scaffold)

```txt
src/
  index.ts · client.ts · server.ts · metadata.ts
  __CODE__-core.contract.ts
  __CODE__-example.command.server.ts
  __CODE__-example.handler.server.ts
  __CODE__-example.schema.ts
  __CODE__-example.read-model.server.ts
  __CODE__-example.component.client.tsx
```

No bucket folders (`commands/`, `schemas/`, …) in new packages.

### Naming

```txt
{code}-{topic}.{artifact}.{canonical}.{ext}
```

- **code** — first 3 alphanumeric chars of module id (`purchasing` → `pur`, `lynx` → `lyn`)
- **topic** — kebab-case subject (`order-create`, `truth-search`)
- **artifact** — `command` · `handler` · `contract` · `schema` · `read-model` · `policy` · `repository` · `domain` · `component` · …
- **canonical** — optional `server` · `client` · `types` · `shared`

Examples:

- `pur-order-create.command.server.ts`
- `pur-order.schema.ts`
- `lyn-truth-search.handler.server.ts`

## Vertical slice (group by capability name only)

```bash
pnpm scaffold:vertical __MODULE_ID__ <capability>
```

```txt
src/<capability>/
  index.ts
  __CODE__-<capability>-example.command.server.ts
  __CODE__-<capability>-example.handler.server.ts
  ...
```

Still flat inside the slice folder — **no** nested buckets.

## Constraints

- **Only** place for `@afenda/feature-__MODULE_ID__` module business truth (**ARCH-1002** §6).
- Import public doors only — never deep paths from app or other packages.
- No catch-all folders (`_shared`, `common`, `lib`, `utils`, `helpers`, `misc`).
- `@afenda/db` owns schema; feature owns queries and domain.

## After scaffold

1. Add `__MODULE_ID__` to `packages/config/src/module-ids.ts` when it is a workspace module route.
2. Add `@afenda/feature-__MODULE_ID__` to `packages/config/src/next.ts` `afendaTranspilePackages`.
3. Add workspace dep in `apps/erp/package.json`.
4. Run `pnpm architecture:check`.
